From 763d468769269084af3a8f63ae0ff3527627f69c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vincent <vincent@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 07:11:16 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] gateway: an uncounted prompt reads beside its conversation's
 counted prompts (#3169)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A request the agent cancelled (a 499: "the agent canceled the request") comes
back with no vendor usage, so `promptCounted` is 0 and `calibrate` returns
before scaling: the card shows the estimator's own reading, about four
characters a token. On a body that tokenizes lower — Grok CLI's, on two
vendors — that reading is 1.5 to 1.6 times every counted request around it in
the same conversation, every part inflated alike, so a 323K prompt's
cancelled neighbour read 525,109 and looked like a context blow-up (Sealt:
system 1,209 → 1,961, tools 6,228 → 10,104, chat 203,407 → 330,164 across 18
seconds of one turn).

The estimate is now scaled by the factor the conversation's last counted
prompt was scaled by, the same agent's session (or, an agent that names no
session, its first turn): the trace keeps what the estimator read of each body
(`Prompt.Est`), so that factor is what the vendor counted of the neighbour
over what was estimated of its body. `trace.promptShown` is the one place a
route's prompt is put in the trace, for the gateway's own requests and
Codex's backend path alike. Nothing to scale to — the conversation's first
request, or one whose counted requests the trace no longer holds — keeps the
plain estimate. The card still says Estimated: nothing is counted.

RED, on the clean base with the fix stashed and the test kept: the reporter's
two-request shape through the real handler, one vendor-counted request and one
cancelled in the same conversation, `go test ./internal/gateway -run
TestUncountedPromptReadsBesideItsCountedNeighbour -count=1` fails in 0.02s —
"the cancelled request reads 3410 tokens against 2103 counted beside it; want
1752 to 2453" (1.62x). GREEN with the fix: ok in 0.02s, and the same band on
each part that cannot have grown (system, tools) with every other part keeping
its share of the estimate.

Ran: `go test ./internal/gateway -count=1` ok except
TestClaudeClientCacheAbsentUnchanged, red on the clean base too (a real
`claude` binary's args in this environment, unrelated). `gofmt -l
internal/gateway` clean. `go vet ./...`, `GOOS=linux GOARCH=amd64 go vet -tags
nogui ./...`, `GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go vet ./...`, `go build ./...`,
`GOOS=linux GOARCH=amd64 go build -tags nogui ./...` and `GOOS=windows
GOARCH=amd64 go build ./...` all exit 0.

Not verified: the Routing page itself in a browser. No page code changed — the
card reads the tokens this now scales, and its Estimated label is untouched.

Fixes #3169
